{
  "title": "Intrinsic Minus Hand (Claw Hand)",
  "url": "https://www.orthobullets.com/hand/6010/intrinsic-minus-hand-claw-hand",
  "subtitle": "Updated: Feb 18 2025",
  "sections": [
    {
      "text": "Summary",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Intrinsic Minus Hand is a hand deformity characterized by MCP joint hyperextension with PIP joint and DIP joint flexion caused by an imbalance between strong extrinsics and deficient intrinsics.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "5",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Diagnosis is made by clinical exam which shows MCP hyperextension and IP joint flexion which corrects when the MCP joint is brought out from hyperextension.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Treatment may be nonoperative or operative depending on the severity of the contracture and impact on quality of life.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Etiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "-1",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Pathophysiology",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "**ulnar nerve palsy**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "cubital tunnel syndrome",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "ulnar tunnel syndrome",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "**median nerve palsy**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "Volkmann's ischemic contracture",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "leprosy (Hansen's disease)",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "failure to splint the hand in an intrinsic-plus posture following a crush injury",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "Charcot-Marie-Tooth disease (hereditary motor-sensory neuropathy)",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "compartment syndrome of the hand",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Pathoanatomy",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Pathoanatomic components",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "**loss of intrinsics**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "leads to loss of baseline MCP flexion and loss of IP extension",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "**strong extrinsic EDC**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "leads to unopposed extension of the MCP joint",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "remember the EDC is not a significant extensor of the PIP joint",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "most of the MCP extension forces on the terminal insertion of the central slip come from the interosseous muscles",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "**strong FDP and FDS**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [
                {
                  "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/6010/images/intrinsic%20modified.jpg",
                  "caption": "Shows pathoanatomy"
                }
              ],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "leads to unopposed flexion of the PIP and DIP",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Presentation",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Symptoms",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "decreased hand function",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Physical exam",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "**MCP hyperextension and IP joint flexion**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [
                {
                  "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/6010/images/claw-hand_moved.jpg",
                  "caption": ""
                }
              ],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "with an ulnar nerve palsy, the deformity will be worse in the 4th and 5th digits (lumbricals innervated by the ulnar nerve)",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "not as severe in the 2nd and 3rd digits (lumbricals innervated by the median nerve)",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "**functional weakness**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "unable to perform prehensile grasp",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "diminished grip and pinch strength",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "provocative tests",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "**Bouvier's Test: MCP joint is passively brought out of hyperextension**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "If PIP joint extension returns (positive) - simple claw hand",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "If PIP joint extension does not return (negative) - complex claw hand",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Treatment",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Operative",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "contracture release and passive tenodesis vs. active tendon transfer",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "progressive deformity that is affecting quality of life",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "technique",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "goal is to **prevent MCP joint hyperextension**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
